---
pagination:
  data: paperPages
  size: 1
  alias: paper
  # Eleventy adds only a paginated template's FIRST page to collections.all,
  # which is what sitemap.xml.njk walks, so 314 of these 315 pages were absent
  # from the sitemap the site submits to search engines (#1293). These pages
  # exist to be indexed: they carry the citation_* meta, the ScholarlyArticle
  # JSON-LD and now the .bib/.ris siblings. The .bib and .ris templates stay
  # out via eleventyExcludeFromCollections, since a citation file is not a page.
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
layout: base.njk
permalink: "/papers/{{ paper.slug }}.html"
navKey: "navigator"
eleventyComputed:
  title: "{{ paper.title }}"
  description: "{{ (paper.abstract or paper.title) | striptags | truncate(155) }}"
---
{# Per-paper landing page (#794). One template paginates over paperPages to
   emit /papers/<slug>.html for every abstract- or published-link-bearing
   ESSC paper, EN-only. The citation_* meta tags live in base.njk's <head>
   (it reads the `paper` alias); this body carries the human-readable record
   plus the ScholarlyArticle JSON-LD. #}
{% include "paper-page-body.njk" %}
